+# Agent Note: Automatic continuation after output-token truncation
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-20-max-token-continuation.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+A conversation model can spend an entire per-request output budget on reasoning or a long answer and finish with `max-tokens` before completing the task. The durable partial output is useful, but requiring a human to submit “continue” turns an expected model limit into manual supervision and leaves long-running tasks stalled.
+
+## Decision
+
+The shipped base composition mounts [`@deepseek-ai/dsh-max-token-continuation`](../../../../packages/guard/max-token-continuation/README.md) in the host plane. The plugin listens to durable `turn/end` events and, for `max-tokens`, queues one ordinary next-turn message through `agent.followup()`. Every later max-token ending repeats the same operation without a plugin-level round cap; any non-max-token ending stops the chain naturally.
+
+The message is plugin-sourced, retained as `user/message`, and contains exactly:
+
+```markdown
+<system-reminder>
+上一轮因输出 token 上限被截断，已有输出已保留，从停止的位置继续同一个任务。
+</system-reminder>
+```
+
+The plugin reacts only to the typed finish reason. It does not inspect reasoning, parse XML or JSON-like text, recover partial tool-call arguments, or execute any tool call. The LLM assembler remains responsible for dropping unfinished tool-call blocks before the safe assistant prefix is committed.
+
+## Turn ownership and takeover
+
+The session publishes `turn/end` inside append publication, where a nested durable inbox write is forbidden. The listener records continuation intent without writing. When the exact live agent enters `idle`, the plugin rechecks competing `nextTurn` work and then calls `followup()`; this replacement activity is tracked by `whenIdle()`. Existing `nextTurn` work takes precedence. Input submitted after the continuation request starts follows normal steering and cancellation semantics.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Teach the Web client to submit “continue”.** This would duplicate host lifecycle policy in one client, fail for headless and SDK callers, and make replay depend on UI timing.
+
+**Parse tool-call markup from truncated reasoning and execute it.** A truncated payload is not a trustworthy tool request, and textual examples are indistinguishable from intent without model-native structure. Executing it would turn presentation text into authority.
+
+**Change the core agent loop.** The loop already exposes the durable session event and public inbox operation needed for continuation. A host plugin keeps the mechanism composable and avoids adding policy to the driver.
+
+**Cap automatic continuation rounds.** A fixed cap merely moves the manual stall to a later request and has no task-independent correct value. Unlimited continuation matches the requested unattended behavior; cancellation and human takeover are the explicit controls.
+
+## Verification
+
+Package tests run the real agent loop against a keyless scripted adapter and cover repeated max-token endings, eventual normal completion, already queued human work, request failure, and plugin disposal. The shipped Web composition test boots the built bundle and snapshots two automatic continuations before completion. Client rendering tests pin the shortened truncation notice.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Long reasoning tasks continue without human input, and each partial assistant response plus reminder remains reconstructable from the event log. Requests stay prefix-stable for KV Cache reuse because the system prompt and earlier messages do not change; the retained partial output and reminder extend the tail. A model that perpetually reaches its output limit can issue unbounded requests until cancellation, failure, disposal, competing work, or another non-max-token ending intervenes.
