+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-max-token-continuation
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+This host-plane guard resumes the same agent task when a conversation request ends at its output-token limit. It listens for a durable `turn/end` with reason `max-tokens`, queues one plugin-sourced next-turn message through `agent.followup()`, and repeats on every later max-token ending without a round cap. A normal completion, request error, cancellation, disposal, or competing next-turn message ends this automatic chain. The decision is recorded in the [max-token continuation Agent Note](../../../.agents/notes/implemented/feature/2026-08-20-max-token-continuation.md).
+
+## Continuation semantics
+
+The plugin never parses assistant reasoning or visible text and never reconstructs or executes a truncated tool call. The LLM assembler and agent loop retain safe text and reasoning while dropping unfinished tool-call blocks before `turn/end`; this guard reacts only to that durable ending and starts an ordinary new turn.
+
+The max-token event records continuation intent without writing during session publication. When the agent reaches idle, already queued ordinary next-turn work takes precedence and the guard adds nothing; otherwise it queues the reminder and starts the next turn. Input submitted after that request starts follows the normal steering, queueing, and cancellation rules.
+
+The shipped base composition mounts one instance globally. The plugin has no config: unlimited continuation is the product default, while cancellation and human takeover remain the runtime controls.
+
+## Model Experience
+
+### Max-token continuation message
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+The next request retains the truncated assistant output and appends the following plugin-sourced user-role message. The system prompt and request header are unchanged.
+
+##### Continuation reminder
+
+```markdown
+<system-reminder>
+上一轮因输出 token 上限被截断，已有输出已保留，从停止的位置继续同一个任务。
+</system-reminder>
+```
+
+#### Token effect
+
+Each max-token ending adds one retained reminder and another conversation request. Repeated max-token endings have no package-level round cap; ordinary context compaction still applies before later requests.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Append-only. The existing system prompt, tool schemas, and message prefix remain byte-identical; each reminder and retained partial response extend the request tail.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- **A claimed continuation is already running work** — a human follow-up submitted after the reminder enters its turn does not retroactively replace that request; steering or cancellation provides immediate takeover.
+- **Unlimited continuation can consume unbounded requests** — a model that repeatedly reaches its output-token ceiling continues until another terminal condition or operator action occurs; a fixed retry cap is deliberately not imposed.
